======= EXECUTABLE CHECK =======

---- ../bfdctl -C bfdd.sock --help

../bfdctl: invalid option -- '-'
bfdctl: [OPTIONS...]
	-C: control socket path
	-M: monitor (show notifications for all peers or a specific)
	-a: add peer
	-d: delete peer
	-L <label>: when deleting, find peer by label instead of by address
	-i <ifname>: interface
	-l <address>: local address (e.g. 192.168.0.1 or 2001:db8::100)
	-m: multihop
	-p <address>: peer address (e.g. 192.168.0.1 or 2001:db8::100)
	-v: verbose mode
======= CONTROL SOCKET CHECK =======

---- ../bfdctl -C bfdd.sock -M

Response:
{
  "status":"ok"
}

---- ../bfdctl -C bfdd.sock -M m

Response:
{
  "status":"ok"
}
